From ba4de177bd4a89aac65a63071ce8bbd1d351ae7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:55:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cron): a gate tick clears a failure streak made only of
 fire/infra refusals [daveey]

hermes-hub cron 6b4342ad83d9 (an unchanged monitor) kept failure_streak 3 after three fires
failed before reaching the agent (GatewayUnavailableError during update restarts): every later
tick was a gate tick, which keeps the last verdict, so the streak stayed >= threshold forever and
coach self_heal never recorded the job fixed. The streak had to be reset by hand.

- Failures that never reached the agent are booked last_error_kind="fire": run_canonical_job's
  pre-submit connect failure, an owner refusal whose recover says missing, and reconcile_pending's
  missing admission (job flag _fire_error -> mark_job_run(fire_error=True)).
- last_error_kind stays "fire" only while every failure in the streak is one; any agent failure
  makes it "agent". A real success clears it.
- A gate tick (agent_skipped) heals a fire-only streak like a success (streak 0, last_status ok,
  alert marker cleared, sticky last_failure kept). Agent verdicts keep today's keep-verdict path.

Tests: tests/cron/test_gated_tick_clears_fire_streak.py (fire booking on both pre-admission paths,
fire-only streak healed by a gate tick, mixed and agent-only streaks kept, success resets the
kind); test_cron_recover_pause asserts the missing-admission kind. RED on origin/main: 6 fail.
---
 cron/jobs.py                                  |  26 ++-
 cron/scheduler_authority.py                   |   4 +-
 cron/scheduler_bookkeeping.py                 |   4 +
 tests/cron/test_cron_recover_pause.py         |   1 +
 .../test_gated_tick_clears_fire_streak.py     | 174 ++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 204 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/cron/test_gated_tick_clears_fire_streak.py

